                <pb facs="0939" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-16T17:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 17—8:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. My telegram number 40, July 19, 6 p.m. Resolution quoted passed Congress this
                    afternoon again by more than two thirds after the President had refused to act
                    upon it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
